{"name":"Relief","hex":"#bf2133","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"relief","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The removal of stress or discomfort.","The feeling associated with the removal of stress or discomfort."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A method of sculpture or other artwork in which shapes or figures protrude from a flat background.","A sculpture or other artwork made with such a method."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/relief"}],"entries":[{"title":"Relief","blocks":[{"text":"Relief is a sculptural method in which the sculpted pieces remain attached to a solid background of the same material. The term relief is from the Latin verb relevare, to raise. To create a sculpture in relief is to give the impression that the sculpted material has been raised above the background plane. When a relief is carved into a flat surface of wood or stone, the field is actually lowered, leaving the unsculpted areas seeming higher. The approach requires chiselling away of the background, which can be time-intensive. On the other hand, a relief saves forming the rear of a subject, and is less fragile and more securely fixed than a sculpture in the round, especially one of a standing figure where the ankles are a potential weak point, particularly in stone. In other materials such as metal, clay, plaster stucco, ceramics or papier-mâché the form can be simply added to or raised up from the background. Monumental bronze reliefs are made by casting."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Abraham_%28Gates_of_Paradise%29_01.JPG/330px-Abraham_%28Gates_of_Paradise%29_01.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Relief","wikidata":"Q245117"},{"title":"Relief (feature selection)","blocks":[{"text":"Relief is an algorithm developed by Kenji Kira and Larry Rendell in 1992 that takes a filter-method approach to feature selection that is notably sensitive to feature interactions. It was originally designed for application to binary classification problems with discrete or numerical features. Relief calculates a feature score for each feature which can then be applied to rank and select top scoring features for feature selection. Alternatively, these scores may be applied as feature weights to guide downstream modeling. Relief feature scoring is based on the identification of feature value differences between nearest neighbor instance pairs. If a feature value difference is observed in a neighboring instance pair with the same class, the feature score decreases. Alternatively, if a feature value difference is observed in a neighboring instance pair with different class values, the feature score increases. The original Relief algorithm has since inspired a family of Relief-based feature selection algorithms (RBAs), including the ReliefF algorithm. Beyond the original Relief algorithm, RBAs have been adapted to (1) perform more reliably in noisy problems, (2) generalize to multi-class problems (3) generalize to numerical outcome problems, and (4) to make them robust to incomplete data."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Relief_(feature_selection)","wikidata":"Q17146113"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Panel_of_Tellus%2C_Ara_Pacis%2C_Rome.jpg/500px-Panel_of_Tellus%2C_Ara_Pacis%2C_Rome.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Panel_of_Tellus%2C_Ara_Pacis%2C_Rome.jpg/1280px-Panel_of_Tellus%2C_Ara_Pacis%2C_Rome.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Panel_of_Tellus%2C_Ara_Pacis%2C_Rome.jpg/500px-Panel_of_Tellus%2C_Ara_Pacis%2C_Rome.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A common mixture of high and low relief, in the Roman Ara Pacis, placed to be seen from below. Low relief background.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APanel_of_Tellus%2C_Ara_Pacis%2C_Rome.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Albert_Memorial_Friese_Facing_South_-_May_2008.jpg/500px-Albert_Memorial_Friese_Facing_South_-_May_2008.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Albert_Memorial_Friese_Facing_South_-_May_2008.jpg/1280px-Albert_Memorial_Friese_Facing_South_-_May_2008.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Albert_Memorial_Friese_Facing_South_-_May_2008.jpg/500px-Albert_Memorial_Friese_Facing_South_-_May_2008.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A face of the high-relief Frieze of Parnassus round the base of the Albert Memorial in London. Most of the heads and many feet are completely undercut, but the torsos are \"engaged\" with the surface behind.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAlbert_Memorial_Friese_Facing_South_-_May_2008.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/63/PupienusSest.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/63/PupienusSest.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Low-relief on Roman sestertius, 238 AD","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APupienusSest.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Rock_Relief_of_Iddin-Sin%2C_King_of_Simurrum.jpg/500px-Rock_Relief_of_Iddin-Sin%2C_King_of_Simurrum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Rock_Relief_of_Iddin-Sin%2C_King_of_Simurrum.jpg/1280px-Rock_Re